Registration of the new "e10_batch_audit" reward manager and the new
"compute_score_em_batch_e10" scorer is achieved entirely through:
  1. A PYTHONPATH-prepended sitecustomize.py (auto-imported by the Python
     interpreter at startup in every process that inherits this PYTHONPATH,
     including Ray workers via OS-level env inheritance), which imports
     e10_reward_manager.py and thereby runs its own `@register("e10_batch_audit")`
     decorator -- a mechanism the original verl reward-manager registry
     (verl/verl/workers/reward_manager/__init__.py + registry.py) already
     exposes for exactly this purpose. No import or edit was added to that
     original registry file.
  2. Hydra CLI overrides passed on the command line
     (reward_model.reward_manager=e10_batch_audit,
     custom_reward_function.train_path=.../e10_scorer.py,
     custom_reward_function.train_name=compute_score_em_batch_e10), which is
     the exact mechanism train_dapo_mhqa_agent_wiki.sh already uses to select
     reward_model.reward_manager=batch / custom_reward_function.train_name=
     compute_score_em_batch in the original run -- E1-0 uses the identical
     mechanism with different values, not a new code path.

